  "isAvailable": true,
  "caption": "This little comet wears its tail like a scarf 🧣\n\nYou're looking at a photo of comet Example-7. This icy wanderer is only around 4 miles across—about the length of a small harbor town. It hides frozen gas below a dusty crust, and as it nears the Sun that gas boils off into space.\n\nThe comet may be small, but it’s mighty enough to stretch a tail for millions of miles. The dust it sheds drifts along its path and, years later, lights up a meteor shower.\n\nThe filters on our survey telescope give the tail a soft teal hue. In reality, it is a pale grey-white.\n\nCredit: Orbit Lab\n\n#OrbitLab #Comet #NightSky #Telescope",
